            <ArticleTitle>[Liver torsion leading to death in a 16-month-old infant treated neonatally for an omphalocele].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>260-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.arcped.2011.12.019</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of an infant who underwent surgery on the first day of life for a giant omphalocele. At the age of 16 months, he presented an acute abdominal syndrome and died a few hours later. Autopsy revealed a twisted left liver lobe (LL) including a suprahepatic vein. To our knowledge, this is the first case of giant omphalocele complicated by twisted liver lobe and fatal outcome.</AbstractText>
